    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d560">

                <pb facs="0710" n="598" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg598"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 711.12/132</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Stewart</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1922</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Vera Cruz</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-26">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 26, 1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith an
                    editorial, with translation, on President Wilson, published on July 25 in <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Los Sucesos</hi> of Vera Cruz, which is the best
                    appreciation of Mr. Wilson’s policy by a Mexican that I have ever seen published
                    in a Vera Cruz paper.</p>
                <pb facs="0711" n="599" xml:id="pg599"/>
                <p>I am confidentially informed that “Renato” is the pseudonym of the local
                    postmaster.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Francis R. Stewart</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d560-a1.xml" xpointer="d560-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
